; ─── compile-bytes : Bytes → Bytes (the pipeline; the harness/ABI entry) ────────
; ⚠ SINGLE-ENTRY PIPELINE — TO BE REPLACED (user directive 2026-07-08; task #16).
; This runs ONE resolve-program→…→wrap-component for a single `main`. The ratified
; model is MULTI-EXPORT: resolve collects `(export name…)`, a layout carries EVERY
; export by SIGNATURE, and the frame emits the N-export envelope mechanically (mirror
; rcdzc — seed/crates/rcdzc/{resolve,layout,component,serialize}.rs). The single-`run`
; envelope in the @generated 40-frame.cdz (fix its generator xtask/src/frame.rs) is
; part of what's replaced. See 20-resolve.cdz's header flag for the full picture.
(def (compile-bytes b)
  (doc "The whole pipeline: `decode` the program bytes to an Ast with our own recursive-descent parser
        (NOT a runtime `Ast.decode` host op — ask-69 retired), resolve → Hir, lower → Mir, eval-mir,
        select → a flat `list Lir` body (threading scratch-local slots from 0), serialize-body → bytes,
        and frame the scalar component with the body's scratch-local count. A scalar `main` needs 0 scratch
        locals; a checked arithmetic op needs 3 per op (see mir-scratch-count). Any unhandled shape lowers
        to MError → `unreachable` (a clean decline trap), still a valid component.")
  (let ((m (eval-mir (lower (resolve-program (decode b))))))
    (wrap-component (core-module-locals (serialize-body (select m 0)) (mir-scratch-count m)))))
